      "summary": "NAURA Technology Group cracks key 3D DRAM etching process; CXMT climbs to fourth in global market share finance.biggo.com",
      "body": "NAURA Technology Group cracks key 3D DRAM etching process; CXMT climbs to fourth in global market share\nNAURA Technology Group, China's leading semiconductor equipment maker, published an academic paper in an IEEE journal unveiling a critical process breakthrough for next-generation 3D DRAM memory chip manufacturing—a two-step cyclic etching technique. The technology specifically addresses the high-aspect-ratio selective etching challenges encountered when memory chips transition from two-dimensional planar designs to three-dimensional stacking, enabling critical fabrication steps to be completed without EUV (extreme ultraviolet) lithography equipment.\nThe timing of the announcement is notably significant. Just before and after the paper's publication, CXMT delivered an impressive market performance. According to Counterpoint Research's global DRAM market analysis, total global DRAM market revenue rose 385% year-over-year in the second quarter of 2026, with a 57% sequential increase. C",
